Note: reproduced from Muthukumarasamy et al.
41
Neuroimaging findings: axial computed tomography (CT) scan (
A
) showing sulcal calcifications (arrowheads) and obstructive hydrocephalus upon the initial presentation. Images
B–F
are from a subsequent brain and whole spine magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scan. Fluid-attenuated inversion recovery (FLAIR) sequence (
B
) demonstrating ventricular dilatation with associated periventricular hyperintensity. The thin arrows highlight ependymal hyperintensity on the precontrast T1-weighted image (
C
), with corresponding enhancement on the gadolinium-enhanced T1-weighted sequence (
D
). Thick arrows in the contrast-enhanced brain (
E
) and spine (
F
) images demonstrating extensive leptomeningeal enhancement.
